# The append-only logs (ADR 81): two branches that each appended an entry
# merge by keeping both, instead of conflicting on the shared end of the file.
# A duplicate the union leaves behind (two ADRs given one number) is caught by
# the pre-merge decisions-log gate, not by git.
# ROADMAP.md is only append-only in its Results log, but an attribute names a
# whole file: a concurrent edit to its other sections also merges by union.
docs/decisions.md merge=union
docs/ROADMAP.md merge=union
docs/implementations/** merge=union
docs/learnings/** merge=union
# The debt index only grows at its end and a resolution is a row of its own
# (ADR 297), so two branches that each appended merge by keeping both. A row
# both sides edited in place would be kept twice: the pre-merge debt-index gate
# catches that, not git.
docs/debt/README.md merge=union
docs/debt/log.md merge=union
